OmaWhatsApp dependency patch 3 of 3: downstream outcomes (omawhatsapp.3).

Not upstream code. Apply to upstream openclaw/wacli
b87e6178b7b1e571ce2821ab516039cfa0c6ecf6 after wacli-private-input.patch
and wacli-send-queue.patch. git apply ignores this header. Each change is
OmaWhatsApp-specific:

1. App-state read marks bypass the send slot (cmd/wacli/send_ipc.go).
   chats mark-read and mark-unread without --receipts can wait minutes on
   app-state recovery, and the app already serializes them on its own
   chat-state slot; in the send slot they held up interactive sends.
   Receipt-mode read marks never enter recovery and stay serialized and
   paced, as upstream keeps them. The bypass and writeDelegateResult follow
   upstream bb80227 (#454), which does the same for chat_state. A read mark
   can now overlap a reconnect started by a failed send; it then fails like
   any other read-mark failure and can be repeated. Behaviour by Brunno Vert
   (OmaWhatsApp #28).
2. Fixed private-mode outcomes (omawhatsapp_outcomes.go, root.go,
   send_ipc.go). Private input replaces every error with "Private WhatsApp
   command failed.", which hid upstream's "it was not sent" and "may still
   have gone through" reports (#456). The daemon's exact pre-dispatch
   refusals now print "Private WhatsApp command was not sent."; a request
   that failed after dispatch at its deadline, an unanswered delegate and
   any other deadline print "Private WhatsApp command outcome is unknown."
   Both are fixed strings: no socket path, wrapped error, identifier or
   content. The store-lock message is unchanged and takes precedence.
3. A send attempt's own 45s deadline counts as a deadline
   (send_helpers.go). OmaWhatsApp gives file, voice and sticker sends 120s,
   and an attempt cut at 45s after its frame was written was reported as a
   definite failure. The text is unchanged; the error now unwraps to
   context.DeadlineExceeded, so upstream's wrapping reports it as uncertain.
4. --private-args-version adds "build":"omawhatsapp.3" (main.go). Probes
   that read only protocol and max_bytes are unaffected.
5. Tests: omawhatsapp_send_latency_test.go (from OmaWhatsApp #28, with a
   receipt-mode case added) and omawhatsapp_outcomes_test.go.

